1
00:02:40,720 --> 00:02:42,260
I'm so sorry, my queen.

2
00:02:43,550 --> 00:02:45,140
He was a good man.

3
00:02:45,140 --> 00:02:47,480
"Barristan the Bold" They called him.

4
00:02:48,700 --> 00:02:51,040
He crossed a continent to serve me.

5
00:02:52,070 --> 00:02:53,550
He was a loyal friend.

6
00:02:55,730 --> 00:02:57,470
And he died in an alley,

7
00:02:58,120 --> 00:03:01,110
butchered by cowards who hide behind masks.

8
00:03:03,950 --> 00:03:06,130
We could pull back to the pyramid district,

9
00:03:06,670 --> 00:03:10,050
secure it, and use it as a base from which to operate.

10
00:03:10,050 --> 00:03:13,590
Then we clean the city out,

11
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:16,910
neighborhood by neighborhood, street by street,

12
00:03:16,910 --> 00:03:19,420
until the rats have nowhere left to hide.

13
00:03:23,010 --> 00:03:24,860
I prefer your earlier suggestion.

14
00:03:25,680 --> 00:03:28,040
Round up the leaders of each of Meereen's great families

15
00:03:28,040 --> 00:03:29,440
and bring them to me.

16
00:03:31,140 --> 00:03:34,540
But I'm the leader of my family.

17
00:03:37,570 --> 00:03:38,620
No, Your Grace!

18
00:03:39,190 --> 00:03:40,900
I had nothing to do with this.

19
00:03:41,580 --> 00:03:42,480
Your Grace!

20
00:06:14,360 --> 00:06:15,890
Don't want to overfeed them.

21
00:06:20,060 --> 00:06:21,460
Tomorrow perhaps.

22
00:06:57,920 --> 00:07:01,270
"And though Daenerys maintains her grip on Slaver's Bay,

23
00:07:01,270 --> 00:07:04,720
forces rise against her from within and without.

24
00:07:04,730 --> 00:07:08,800
She refuses to leave until the freedom of the former slaves is secure."

25
00:07:10,970 --> 00:07:12,780
She sounds like quite a woman.

26
00:07:12,780 --> 00:07:14,110
And she's alone,

27
00:07:14,510 --> 00:07:15,780
under siege,

28
00:07:16,200 --> 00:07:19,440
no family to guide her or protect her.

29
00:07:19,950 --> 00:07:23,580
Her last relation thousands of miles away,

30
00:07:24,340 --> 00:07:27,400
useless, dying.

31
00:07:29,140 --> 00:07:31,580
Don't say that, Maester Aemon.

32
00:07:31,580 --> 00:07:35,650
A Targaryen alone in the world

33
00:07:37,210 --> 00:07:38,940
is a terrible thing.

34
00:07:42,510 --> 00:07:43,650
Maester Aemon.

35
00:07:44,340 --> 00:07:45,730
Lord Commander.

36
00:07:46,770 --> 00:07:49,120
Sam, I'd like to speak to the maester alone.

37
00:08:04,870 --> 00:08:05,950
How are you feeling?

38
00:08:06,540 --> 00:08:08,870
Oh, like a hundred-year-old man

39
00:08:08,870 --> 00:08:11,190
slowly freezing to death.

40
00:08:15,830 --> 00:08:17,110
I need your advice.

41
00:08:18,940 --> 00:08:20,800
There's something I want to do, something I...

42
00:08:21,540 --> 00:08:22,940
have to do.

43
00:08:22,940 --> 00:08:24,850
But it'll divide the Night's Watch.

44
00:08:25,770 --> 00:08:26,740
Bitterly.

45
00:08:26,740 --> 00:08:29,570
Half the men will hate me the moment I give the order.

46
00:08:30,340 --> 00:08:33,890
Half the men hate you already, Lord Commander.

47
00:08:33,900 --> 00:08:34,710
Do it.

48
00:08:36,260 --> 00:08:37,250
But you don't know what it is.

49
00:08:37,250 --> 00:08:39,160
That doesn't matter.

50
00:08:39,650 --> 00:08:40,760
You do.

51
00:08:43,950 --> 00:08:48,050
You will find little joy in your command.

52
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:50,280
But with luck,

53
00:08:50,280 --> 00:08:54,090
you will find the strength to do what needs to be done.

54
00:08:55,980 --> 00:08:58,870
Kill the boy, Jon Snow.

55
00:09:00,020 --> 00:09:02,460
Winter is almost upon us.

56
00:09:03,450 --> 00:09:04,730
Kill the boy

57
00:09:06,020 --> 00:09:08,760
and let the man be born.

58
00:09:18,030 --> 00:09:20,060
Where are the rest of the free folk now?

59
00:09:20,910 --> 00:09:22,080
Where have they gone?

60
00:09:26,780 --> 00:09:28,200
Who leads them?

61
00:09:28,950 --> 00:09:30,480
They followed Mance.

62
00:09:31,260 --> 00:09:33,330
They won't follow anyone else.

63
00:09:36,620 --> 00:09:37,710
What about you?

64
00:09:40,070 --> 00:09:42,140
Hard to lead when you're in chains.

65
00:09:46,260 --> 00:09:47,830
What if I unchained you?

66
00:09:47,830 --> 00:09:49,080
Why would you do that?

67
00:09:51,180 --> 00:09:52,980
Because you are not my enemy.

68
00:09:54,150 --> 00:09:55,380
And I'm not yours.

69
00:09:55,380 --> 00:09:58,310
You sure seemed like my enemy when you were killing my friends.

70
00:09:58,310 --> 00:10:00,990
For 8,000 years the Night's Watch have sworn an oath

71
00:10:00,990 --> 00:10:03,520
to be the shield that guards the realms of men.

72
00:10:05,530 --> 00:10:09,040
And for 8,000 years we've fallen short of that oath.

73
00:10:09,040 --> 00:10:10,890
You belong to the realms of men.

74
00:10:11,820 --> 00:10:12,850
All of you.

75
00:10:13,640 --> 00:10:16,230
And now everything is going to change?

76
00:10:16,790 --> 00:10:18,690
- It is. - Why now?

77
00:10:18,700 --> 00:10:22,530
Because now I am Lord Commander of the Night's Watch.

78
00:10:23,230 --> 00:10:24,900
What would you have me do,

79
00:10:25,920 --> 00:10:27,880
Lord Commander?

80
00:10:29,810 --> 00:10:31,410
I'd have you go north of the Wall.

81
00:10:32,040 --> 00:10:34,540
Gather the remaining free folk wherever they are

82
00:10:34,540 --> 00:10:35,890
and bring them back here.

83
00:10:36,290 --> 00:10:38,510
I'll open the gates for them and let them through.

84
00:10:39,620 --> 00:10:42,270
I'll find them lands to settle south of the Wall.

85
00:10:42,270 --> 00:10:46,080
They won't kneel for you and neither will I.

86
00:10:46,080 --> 00:10:48,240
I don't want them to kneel for me.

87
00:10:48,850 --> 00:10:51,520
I want them to fight with me when the time comes.

88
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:54,230
The day I ask my people to fight with the crows

89
00:10:54,280 --> 00:10:57,010
is the day my people cut my guts from my belly

90
00:10:57,010 --> 00:10:58,500
and make me eat them.

91
00:10:58,500 --> 00:11:00,850
And how many of your people can't fight?

92
00:11:01,540 --> 00:11:04,160
The women, the children, the old, the sick--

93
00:11:04,160 --> 00:11:05,510
what happens to them?

94
00:11:06,110 --> 00:11:07,910
You're condemning them to death.

95
00:11:08,410 --> 00:11:09,730
Worse than death

96
00:11:09,730 --> 00:11:12,350
because you're too proud to make peace.

97
00:11:15,710 --> 00:11:17,340
Or maybe you're not proud.

98
00:11:19,610 --> 00:11:21,220
Maybe you're just a coward.

99
00:11:28,240 --> 00:11:31,110
Easy thing to say to a man in chains.

100
00:11:55,740 --> 00:11:57,390
Your people need a leader.

101
00:11:57,680 --> 00:12:00,880
And they need to get south of the Wall before it's too late.

102
00:12:00,880 --> 00:12:02,730
We don't have much time and they have less.

103
00:12:02,730 --> 00:12:05,650
The walkers are coming and they'll hit your people first.

104
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:10,260
I'm not asking you to make peace to save your skin.

105
00:12:10,560 --> 00:12:14,090
Make peace to save your people.

106
00:12:22,640 --> 00:12:24,440
Most of them are at Hardhome.

107
00:12:25,160 --> 00:12:26,360
You know where that is?

108
00:12:26,360 --> 00:12:28,060
Up on Storrold's Point.

109
00:12:28,060 --> 00:12:30,310
I can give you 10 horses and nine other men.

110
00:12:30,310 --> 00:12:32,170
You can get there in a week.

111
00:12:32,170 --> 00:12:33,770
We'll need ships.

112
00:12:35,240 --> 00:12:38,040
I'll talk to King Stannis about lending you his fleet.

113
00:12:41,480 --> 00:12:42,820
All right, then.

114
00:12:45,270 --> 00:12:46,690
You're coming with me.

115
00:12:48,010 --> 00:12:50,720
You're the Lord Commander of the Night's Watch.

116
00:12:50,980 --> 00:12:52,720
They need to hear it from you.

117
00:12:53,010 --> 00:12:55,370
They need to know the ships they are boarding

118
00:12:55,370 --> 00:12:57,730
wot be torched in the middle of the sea.

119
00:12:58,090 --> 00:13:02,490
You come with me or I don't go.

120
00:13:10,540 --> 00:13:13,350
You'd bring wildlings here through our gates?

121
00:13:13,350 --> 00:13:15,100
Men, women, and children

122
00:13:15,100 --> 00:13:17,240
will die by the thousands if we do nothing.

123
00:13:17,240 --> 00:13:20,200
Let them die. We got our own to worry about.

124
00:13:20,430 --> 00:13:21,970
Less enemies for us.

125
00:13:23,620 --> 00:13:24,600
Fewer.

126
00:13:25,280 --> 00:13:27,500
- What? - Nothing.

127
00:13:28,080 --> 00:13:31,980
Look, well, there is good farmland in the Gift.

128
00:13:32,340 --> 00:13:34,140
Land that no one uses now.

129
00:13:34,420 --> 00:13:35,650
A dozen abandoned villages.

130
00:13:35,650 --> 00:13:38,700
And why do you think the farmers abandoned those villages?

131
00:13:38,960 --> 00:13:41,340
Because the wildlings raided them for years.

132
00:13:41,910 --> 00:13:43,110
Cut them down.

133
00:13:43,540 --> 00:13:46,960
- Just like they did this boy's people. - Aye!

134
00:13:48,350 --> 00:13:51,450
We've been fighting them for thousands of years.

135
00:13:51,660 --> 00:13:53,610
They've slaughtered villages.

136
00:13:54,020 --> 00:13:56,010
They've slaughtered our brothers.

137
00:13:56,010 --> 00:13:57,600
And we've slaughtered theirs.

138
00:13:59,720 --> 00:14:03,660
I will follow you anywhere, you know that.

139
00:14:04,920 --> 00:14:07,590
- But they killed Grenn. - Yes.

140
00:14:07,590 --> 00:14:09,890
- And they killed Pyp. - Aye.

141
00:14:09,890 --> 00:14:12,550
They killed 50 of our brothers.

142
00:14:12,680 --> 00:14:14,330
I can't forget that.

143
00:14:14,790 --> 00:14:16,240
I can't forgive it.

144
00:14:16,240 --> 00:14:18,380
You were at the Fist of the First Men.

145
00:14:19,010 --> 00:14:21,700
If we abandon them, you know what they become.

146
00:14:21,890 --> 00:14:23,970
We can learn to live with the wildlings

147
00:14:23,970 --> 00:14:26,270
or we can add them to the army of the dead.

148
00:14:26,750 --> 00:14:30,840
Whatever they are now, they're better than that.

149
00:14:59,310 --> 00:15:00,420
Thank you.

150
00:15:01,090 --> 00:15:02,050
Olly.

151
00:15:04,320 --> 00:15:06,550
If you have something you want to say to me,

152
00:15:07,690 --> 00:15:08,760
say it.

153
00:15:15,840 --> 00:15:16,910
It's all right.

154
00:15:19,220 --> 00:15:21,220
You don't mean it, do you?

155
00:15:22,840 --> 00:15:25,210
Telling the wildlings you want to make peace.

156
00:15:25,710 --> 00:15:27,410
You're just doing it to trick them.

157
00:15:28,070 --> 00:15:29,360
It's not a trick.

158
00:15:29,360 --> 00:15:30,910
They burned my village.

159
00:15:30,910 --> 00:15:34,340
They put an arrow through my father's head right in front of me.

160
00:15:34,340 --> 00:15:37,780
They butchered my mother, everyone I ever knew.

161
00:15:45,550 --> 00:15:48,080
I know what it's like to lose the people you love.

162
00:15:50,560 --> 00:15:52,290
I know this is hard for you.

163
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:55,740
But winter is coming.

164
00:15:57,430 --> 00:15:59,100
We know what's coming with it.

165
00:16:00,790 --> 00:16:02,540
We can't face it alone.

166
00:16:08,250 --> 00:16:10,990
Will there be anything else you need, Lord Commander?

167
00:16:14,420 --> 00:16:15,370
No.

168
00:16:49,510 --> 00:16:51,670
She's far away from the Lannisters.

169
00:16:52,810 --> 00:16:54,090
This is her home.

170
00:16:57,220 --> 00:16:59,810
Maybe Lday Sansa's better off here.

171
00:17:00,900 --> 00:17:02,870
Better off with the Boltons

172
00:17:03,030 --> 00:17:05,290
who murdered her mother and brother?

173
00:17:14,170 --> 00:17:17,230
Sansa's in danger even if she doesn't realize it.

174
00:17:31,240 --> 00:17:32,360
Thank you.

175
00:17:34,830 --> 00:17:36,500
You've lived here a long time?

176
00:17:38,540 --> 00:17:39,720
Aye.

177
00:17:40,880 --> 00:17:42,840
Did you know Lord Eddard?

178
00:17:44,620 --> 00:17:46,030
I knew him

179
00:17:47,110 --> 00:17:49,100
and his father before him.

180
00:17:51,300 --> 00:17:53,660
The Starks are gone now.

181
00:17:53,690 --> 00:17:55,330
Not all of them.

182
00:17:55,760 --> 00:17:58,270
I know who's inside that castle.

183
00:17:58,380 --> 00:18:00,150
Everyone knows.

184
00:18:00,370 --> 00:18:01,910
The Boltons.

185
00:18:01,910 --> 00:18:04,210
I'm not talking about the Boltons.

186
00:18:05,360 --> 00:18:07,220
I need to get a message to her.

187
00:18:07,960 --> 00:18:09,790
To Sansa Stark.

188
00:18:11,770 --> 00:18:13,210
Who are you?

189
00:18:13,210 --> 00:18:16,010
Someone who swore to keep her safe.

190
00:18:16,250 --> 00:18:18,100
Swore to who?

191
00:18:18,110 --> 00:18:19,440
Her mother.

192
00:18:20,560 --> 00:18:22,440
Her mother's dead.

193
00:18:22,440 --> 00:18:24,630
That doesn't release me from an oath.

194
00:18:27,890 --> 00:18:30,180
I served Lady Catelyn.

195
00:18:30,800 --> 00:18:32,510
I serve her still.

196
00:18:34,840 --> 00:18:36,490
Who do you serve?

197
00:18:43,550 --> 00:18:44,590
Come back here.

198
00:18:49,060 --> 00:18:50,160
Myranda.

199
00:18:50,460 --> 00:18:52,000
I saw you staring at her.

200
00:18:52,170 --> 00:18:53,770
I'm going to marry her.

201
00:18:54,030 --> 00:18:56,860
That will involve looking at her from time to time.

202
00:19:00,660 --> 00:19:02,290
You said you'd marry me.

203
00:19:03,540 --> 00:19:05,000
And I meant it.

204
00:19:05,300 --> 00:19:07,500
When I was a bastard named Snow.

205
00:19:07,940 --> 00:19:09,270
But I'm a Bolton now.

206
00:19:09,890 --> 00:19:13,100
What I want is no longer the primary consideration.

207
00:19:14,040 --> 00:19:15,930
I'm furthering a dynasty.

208
00:19:19,410 --> 00:19:20,910
Do you think she's pretty?

209
00:19:22,040 --> 00:19:23,330
Of course I do.

210
00:19:23,340 --> 00:19:24,590
I'm not blind.

211
00:19:38,440 --> 00:19:40,130
You think she's pretty, too.

212
00:19:43,510 --> 00:19:45,730
I'm looking forward to our wedding night.

213
00:19:45,730 --> 00:19:49,150
But don't worry, I'll have plenty of time for you.

214
00:19:49,520 --> 00:19:51,470
Perhaps I'll marry, too.

215
00:19:57,030 --> 00:19:59,270
You're the kennel master's daughter.

216
00:19:59,850 --> 00:20:03,240
Who are you going to marry, the stable keeper's son?

217
00:20:09,560 --> 00:20:10,830
You're mine.

218
00:20:12,200 --> 00:20:13,890
You're not going anywhere.

219
00:20:14,560 --> 00:20:16,820
Unless I have to listen to more of your jealousy,

220
00:20:16,820 --> 00:20:19,870
Jealousy bores me. You remember what happens to people who bore me.

221
00:20:22,930 --> 00:20:26,540
You're not going to bore me, are you, Myranda?

222
00:20:45,030 --> 00:20:46,090
Never.

223
00:21:13,740 --> 00:21:15,160
Beg pardon, my lady.

224
00:21:15,160 --> 00:21:17,320
I've come to refill the wash basin.

225
00:21:17,320 --> 00:21:18,830
Oh, I don't need--

226
00:21:20,500 --> 00:21:23,080
You still have friends in the North.

227
00:21:23,080 --> 00:21:24,740
If you're ever in trouble,

228
00:21:24,830 --> 00:21:28,400
light a candle in the highest window of the broken tower.

229
00:21:29,720 --> 00:21:31,910
- But who-- - You're not alone.

230
00:22:10,010 --> 00:22:11,530
I like your dress.

231
00:22:13,720 --> 00:22:15,100
Who made it for you?

232
00:22:15,940 --> 00:22:17,920
I made it myself.

233
00:22:18,080 --> 00:22:19,190
Really?

234
00:22:21,990 --> 00:22:23,480
Who-- who are you?

235
00:22:23,940 --> 00:22:27,260
I'm Myranda, the kennel master's daughter.

236
00:22:30,490 --> 00:22:31,470
May I?

237
00:22:37,910 --> 00:22:39,420
Oh, wonderful.

238
00:22:40,090 --> 00:22:41,660
The stitching.

239
00:22:43,170 --> 00:22:45,320
- Who taught you? - My mother.

240
00:22:46,700 --> 00:22:50,460
I'm sorry for what happened to her.

241
00:22:50,460 --> 00:22:51,600
Thank you.

242
00:22:53,540 --> 00:22:55,100
It's good that she taught you.

243
00:22:55,880 --> 00:22:57,280
It was a gift.

244
00:22:57,290 --> 00:23:01,540
Now every time you wear something you made,

245
00:23:02,040 --> 00:23:03,600
you can remember her.

246
00:23:04,430 --> 00:23:06,120
I'd rather have a mother.

247
00:23:06,120 --> 00:23:08,170
I know. It's not the same.

248
00:23:09,770 --> 00:23:12,270
Still, it's good to remember.

249
00:23:12,880 --> 00:23:14,570
Remember the way things were.

250
00:23:16,760 --> 00:23:18,820
I almost forgot.

251
00:23:19,500 --> 00:23:22,230
There's something else

252
00:23:22,820 --> 00:23:24,570
to help you remember.

253
00:23:34,290 --> 00:23:36,250
Down there at the end.

254
00:23:38,120 --> 00:23:39,350
What is it?

255
00:23:39,500 --> 00:23:41,590
That would spoil the surprise.

256
00:23:42,670 --> 00:23:44,980
Go ahead, it's perfectly safe.

257
00:23:45,950 --> 00:23:48,240
You won't believe it when you see it.

258
00:24:50,750 --> 00:24:51,960
Theon?

259
00:25:01,890 --> 00:25:03,780
You shouldn't be here.

260
00:25:24,550 --> 00:25:28,050
You smell particularly ripe this evening.

261
00:25:30,960 --> 00:25:32,290
Pour me some wine.

262
00:25:57,120 --> 00:25:58,880
Do you have something to tell me?

263
00:26:00,810 --> 00:26:02,070
No, my lord.

264
00:26:02,160 --> 00:26:03,310
Reek.

265
00:26:08,100 --> 00:26:09,310
She saw me.

266
00:26:10,120 --> 00:26:11,140
Who?

267
00:26:11,230 --> 00:26:13,310
Sansa. Lady Sansa.

268
00:26:14,070 --> 00:26:15,600
She came to the kennels.

269
00:26:17,110 --> 00:26:18,420
She saw you?

270
00:26:18,420 --> 00:26:20,670
Yes. I'm sorry, master.

271
00:26:20,870 --> 00:26:22,640
Forgive me. I didn't think...

272
00:26:22,640 --> 00:26:23,750
Come here.

273
00:26:33,030 --> 00:26:35,720
You mustn't keep secrets from me, Reek.

274
00:26:36,210 --> 00:26:37,570
Get on your knees.

275
00:26:50,250 --> 00:26:51,750
Give me your hand.

276
00:27:14,470 --> 00:27:15,850
I forgive you.

277
00:27:27,500 --> 00:27:30,200
I trust you find your chamber suitable, my lady.

278
00:27:30,510 --> 00:27:32,260
Yes, thank you, my lord.

279
00:27:32,440 --> 00:27:33,600
Allow me.

280
00:27:38,170 --> 00:27:39,200
Mother.

281
00:27:39,800 --> 00:27:41,300
Thank you, Ramsay.

282
00:27:51,740 --> 00:27:56,230
My lady, we are all a family, we northerners.

283
00:27:56,690 --> 00:27:59,800
Our blood ties go back thousands of years.

284
00:28:00,160 --> 00:28:03,260
So I'd like to drink to our wedding.

285
00:28:03,380 --> 00:28:06,150
May our happiness spread from Moat Cailin

286
00:28:06,150 --> 00:28:07,560
to the Last Hearth.

287
00:28:08,460 --> 00:28:09,450
To your wedding.

288
00:28:09,510 --> 00:28:10,890
To your wedding.

289
00:28:18,030 --> 00:28:21,140
It must be difficult for you being in a strange place.

290
00:28:21,230 --> 00:28:23,510
This isn't a strange place. This is my home.

291
00:28:24,290 --> 00:28:25,880
It's the people who are strange.

292
00:28:31,110 --> 00:28:31,920
You're right.

293
00:28:32,700 --> 00:28:34,110
Very strange.

294
00:28:37,170 --> 00:28:38,670
More wine, please.

295
00:28:45,720 --> 00:28:48,290
I heard you two had been reunited.

296
00:28:49,140 --> 00:28:50,880
A fitting place for it.

297
00:28:53,250 --> 00:28:55,530
I like to imagine that the last time you spoke

298
00:28:56,250 --> 00:28:57,870
was in this very room.

299
00:29:01,560 --> 00:29:03,360
Are you still angry with him

300
00:29:03,730 --> 00:29:05,040
after he...

301
00:29:10,440 --> 00:29:11,460
what he did?

302
00:29:12,270 --> 00:29:13,380
Don't worry.

303
00:29:13,890 --> 00:29:15,570
The North remembers.

304
00:29:17,310 --> 00:29:18,990
I punished him for it.

305
00:29:19,560 --> 00:29:21,430
He's not ironborn anymore.

306
00:29:22,170 --> 00:29:25,040
Not Theon Greyjoy anymore.

307
00:29:25,130 --> 00:29:26,390
He's a new man.

308
00:29:28,870 --> 00:29:31,070
A new person, anyway.

309
00:29:31,880 --> 00:29:33,110
Aren't you, Reek?

310
00:29:33,590 --> 00:29:34,730
Yes, master.

311
00:29:35,150 --> 00:29:37,600
That's his new name-- Reek.

312
00:29:37,600 --> 00:29:39,020
Why are you doing this?

313
00:29:41,650 --> 00:29:43,400
Because Reek has something to say to you.

314
00:29:44,840 --> 00:29:46,130
Don't you, Reek?

315
00:29:56,530 --> 00:29:57,560
An apology.

316
00:30:04,000 --> 00:30:06,670
Apologize to Lady Sansa for what you did.

317
00:30:08,210 --> 00:30:11,230
Apologize for murding her two brothers.

318
00:30:17,590 --> 00:30:18,410
I'm sorry.

319
00:30:20,470 --> 00:30:21,680
Look at her, Reek.

320
00:30:23,270 --> 00:30:24,890
An apology doesn't mean anything

321
00:30:24,890 --> 00:30:27,260
if you're not looking the person in the eye.

322
00:30:34,240 --> 00:30:36,530
- I'm sorry. - Sorry about what?

323
00:30:38,580 --> 00:30:39,620
For killing your brothers.

324
00:30:50,480 --> 00:30:53,450
There, over and done with.

325
00:30:53,870 --> 00:30:55,880
Doesn't everyone feel better? I do.

326
00:30:56,690 --> 00:30:59,340
That was getting very tense.

327
00:31:05,540 --> 00:31:06,590
You know what, my lady?

328
00:31:08,330 --> 00:31:11,210
What with him having murdered your brothers

329
00:31:11,210 --> 00:31:13,890
and the rest of your family gone...

330
00:31:15,980 --> 00:31:19,910
Reek here is the nearest thing to a living kin

331
00:31:20,120 --> 00:31:21,500
that you have left.

332
00:31:23,150 --> 00:31:24,110
Reek.

333
00:31:25,520 --> 00:31:27,290
You will give away the bride.

334
00:31:30,200 --> 00:31:33,050
Someone has to. What better person?

335
00:31:33,590 --> 00:31:35,270
Good? Good?

336
00:31:36,020 --> 00:31:37,820
Yes, yes, very good.

337
00:31:38,640 --> 00:31:39,740
Wonderful.

338
00:31:42,230 --> 00:31:44,060
Walda and I have some good news as well,

339
00:31:45,050 --> 00:31:46,460
since we're all together.

340
00:31:52,330 --> 00:31:53,860
We're going to have a baby.

341
00:32:00,240 --> 00:32:01,480
I'm very happy for you.

342
00:32:01,810 --> 00:32:03,340
From the way she's carrying,

343
00:32:03,640 --> 00:32:05,860
Maester Wolkan says it looks like a boy.

344
00:32:21,990 --> 00:32:23,220
How can you be sure?

345
00:32:24,510 --> 00:32:25,800
Sure of what?

346
00:32:25,860 --> 00:32:27,210
That she's pregnant.

347
00:32:27,840 --> 00:32:28,890
I mean...

348
00:32:29,910 --> 00:32:31,170
how can you tell?

349
00:32:31,890 --> 00:32:34,540
Maester Wolkan has assured us beyond all doubt.

350
00:32:43,290 --> 00:32:46,470
So how did you manage it?

351
00:32:46,680 --> 00:32:47,940
Manage what?

352
00:32:48,390 --> 00:32:49,920
Getting her pregnant.

353
00:32:50,880 --> 00:32:52,860
I imagine you're familiar with the procedure.

354
00:32:52,860 --> 00:32:56,010
Of course, but how did you...

355
00:32:56,190 --> 00:32:57,360
find it?

356
00:32:57,360 --> 00:32:58,830
You disgraced yourself at dinner

357
00:33:00,120 --> 00:33:02,340
parading that creature before the Stark girl.

358
00:33:02,340 --> 00:33:03,630
And if it's a boy?

359
00:33:07,260 --> 00:33:08,760
You're worried about your position.

360
00:33:08,760 --> 00:33:10,740
My position is quite clear.

361
00:33:11,280 --> 00:33:12,390
I'm your son

362
00:33:13,890 --> 00:33:16,080
until a better alternative comes along.

363
00:33:25,770 --> 00:33:27,330
You've never asked me about your mother.

364
00:33:32,760 --> 00:33:33,690
Why would I?

365
00:33:35,010 --> 00:33:37,230
She had me, she died.

366
00:33:38,730 --> 00:33:40,080
And here we are.

367
00:33:41,610 --> 00:33:43,110
She was peasant girl.

368
00:33:44,250 --> 00:33:46,020
Pretty in a common sort of way.

369
00:33:46,440 --> 00:33:47,760
She was the miller's wife.

370
00:33:48,960 --> 00:33:52,020
Apparently they had married without my knowledge or consent.

371
00:33:52,590 --> 00:33:53,970
So I had him hanged

372
00:33:54,390 --> 00:33:57,040
and I took her beneath the tree where he was swaying.

373
00:33:57,660 --> 00:33:59,310
She fought me the whole time.

374
00:33:59,490 --> 00:34:01,710
She was lucky I didn't hang her, too.

375
00:34:02,460 --> 00:34:04,110
A year later she came to my gates

376
00:34:04,110 --> 00:34:06,420
with a squalling baby in her arms.

377
00:34:06,450 --> 00:34:08,700
A baby she claimed was mine.

378
00:34:08,910 --> 00:34:10,290
I nearly had her whipped

379
00:34:10,680 --> 00:34:12,630
and the child thrown in the river.

380
00:34:18,390 --> 00:34:19,470
But then I looked at you

381
00:34:20,250 --> 00:34:22,470
and I saw then what I see now.

382
00:34:23,250 --> 00:34:24,780
You are my son.

383
00:34:36,960 --> 00:34:39,990
Stannis Baratheon has an army at Castle Black.

384
00:34:40,630 --> 00:34:42,100
But he won't stay for long.

385
00:34:43,510 --> 00:34:45,220
He wants the Iron Throne,

386
00:34:46,360 --> 00:34:49,290
and the road to King's Landing comes right through Winterfell.

387
00:34:50,650 --> 00:34:52,810
He means to take the North.

388
00:34:55,320 --> 00:34:56,830
But the North is ours.

389
00:34:57,520 --> 00:34:59,170
It's yours and mine.

390
00:35:00,910 --> 00:35:02,470
Will you help me defeat him?

391
00:35:05,040 --> 00:35:05,860
Yes.

392
00:35:14,460 --> 00:35:16,210
Is this every book there is?

393
00:35:17,860 --> 00:35:19,180
Every book there is?

394
00:35:20,680 --> 00:35:23,950
- In the world. - Well, no.

395
00:35:23,950 --> 00:35:27,030
There are thousands and thousands of books out there.

396
00:35:28,000 --> 00:35:29,710
This library is rather small, actually.

397
00:35:29,710 --> 00:35:31,810
Where you grew up, were there more books?

398
00:35:31,810 --> 00:35:34,000
My father's not the most literate man.

399
00:35:36,950 --> 00:35:40,780
They say the Citadel has the largest library in the world.

400
00:35:40,780 --> 00:35:41,890
Where's that?

401
00:35:43,660 --> 00:35:44,770
The Citadel?

402
00:35:45,940 --> 00:35:47,440
In Oldtown.

403
00:35:54,310 --> 00:35:56,070
I'm sorry I don't know things.

404
00:35:56,070 --> 00:35:58,440
Gilly, look at me.

405
00:35:59,370 --> 00:36:02,670
You know how to do a hundred things I can never do.

406
00:36:02,670 --> 00:36:04,920
You can build a fire with wet wood.

407
00:36:04,950 --> 00:36:07,730
You can cook. You can stitch a wound.

408
00:36:07,730 --> 00:36:10,490
I can wash the linens. I can sweep the floor.

409
00:36:10,490 --> 00:36:13,950
- Well... - Why does the Citadel have the biggest library?

410
00:36:14,200 --> 00:36:16,840
It's where they train the maesters.

411
00:36:17,110 --> 00:36:18,400
Like Maester Aemon?

412
00:36:18,610 --> 00:36:20,650
I wanted to be one when I was young.

413
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:27,900
Instead, I became a man of the Night's Watch.

414
00:36:31,050 --> 00:36:32,980
Far more adventure up here anyway.

415
00:36:35,340 --> 00:36:36,490
I wouldn't have met you.

416
00:36:43,890 --> 00:36:45,270
Your Grace.

417
00:36:52,710 --> 00:36:54,040
You're Samwell Tarly?

418
00:36:55,750 --> 00:36:57,280
I am, Your Grace.

419
00:36:57,910 --> 00:36:59,710
Your father is Randyll Tarly.

420
00:37:03,030 --> 00:37:05,140
He defeated my brother at the Battle of Ashford.

421
00:37:07,180 --> 00:37:08,890
Only battle Robert ever lost.

422
00:37:10,090 --> 00:37:11,950
I told him he shouldn't go so far west so soon,

423
00:37:11,950 --> 00:37:13,320
but he never listened.

424
00:37:16,140 --> 00:37:17,580
Fine soldier, your father.

425
00:37:19,080 --> 00:37:20,460
You don't look like a soldier.

426
00:37:22,110 --> 00:37:23,910
But I'm told you killed a white walker.

427
00:37:25,170 --> 00:37:26,490
I did, Your Grace.

428
00:37:27,010 --> 00:37:27,900
How?

429
00:37:27,960 --> 00:37:30,060
With a dagger made of dragonglass.

430
00:37:30,240 --> 00:37:31,470
Dragonglass?

431
00:37:31,480 --> 00:37:32,880
What the maesters call obsidian.

432
00:37:32,880 --> 00:37:35,560
I know what it is. We have it in Dragonstone.

433
00:37:35,650 --> 00:37:37,260
Why would obsidian kill a walker?

434
00:37:37,260 --> 00:37:38,470
I don't know.

435
00:37:39,270 --> 00:37:40,830
I've been going through all the old manuscripts

436
00:37:40,830 --> 00:37:43,110
hoping to find something, and all I've learned

437
00:37:43,120 --> 00:37:46,680
is that the children of the forest used to hunt with dragonglass.

438
00:37:46,680 --> 00:37:50,340
The Lady Melisandre told me that death marches on the Wall.

439
00:37:53,790 --> 00:37:55,270
I've seen it, Your Grace.

440
00:37:55,450 --> 00:37:56,610
Seen what?

441
00:37:57,060 --> 00:37:58,810
The army of the dead.

442
00:38:00,180 --> 00:38:03,060
- And when they come-- - We have to know how to fight them.

443
00:38:07,590 --> 00:38:09,480
Keep reading, Samwell Tarly.

444
00:38:27,730 --> 00:38:28,640
It's time.

445
00:38:29,830 --> 00:38:30,950
Uh, Your Grace.

446
00:38:31,950 --> 00:38:33,400
Wouldn't it be better to wait?

447
00:38:33,940 --> 00:38:35,530
When Jon Snow returns with the wildlings,

448
00:38:35,530 --> 00:38:37,090
we could have thousands more men.

449
00:38:37,090 --> 00:38:38,610
If Jon Snow returns with the wildlings.

450
00:38:38,620 --> 00:38:39,970
We can't wait that long.

451
00:38:40,330 --> 00:38:41,670
We have the advantage-- more men,

452
00:38:41,680 --> 00:38:43,810
more horses, all fed and rested.

453
00:38:44,200 --> 00:38:47,070
But every day we wait, the odds shift in Bolton's favor.

454
00:38:47,070 --> 00:38:48,790
This could turn to winter at any moment.

455
00:38:49,060 --> 00:38:50,950
We have to act now. Give the order.

456
00:38:50,950 --> 00:38:52,300
We march at sunrise.

457
00:38:52,390 --> 00:38:54,070
I'll choose a dozen men to stay

458
00:38:54,190 --> 00:38:56,350
and guard the queen and the princess.

459
00:38:56,470 --> 00:38:58,060
No need. They're coming with us.

460
00:39:00,520 --> 00:39:02,380
It's a tough road ahead, Your Grace.

461
00:39:02,590 --> 00:39:04,480
- Won't they be safer-- - Here?

462
00:39:05,470 --> 00:39:08,910
Half these watchmen are killers and rapists.

463
00:39:09,880 --> 00:39:11,980
No, they march with us.

464
00:39:15,390 --> 00:39:16,600
As you wish, Your Grace.

465
00:39:43,010 --> 00:39:45,170
Do you think Father will let me go down into the crypt?

466
00:39:45,170 --> 00:39:46,190
Beg your pardon?

467
00:39:47,060 --> 00:39:48,380
At Winterfell.

468
00:39:48,620 --> 00:39:50,540
All the Kings in the North are buried there.

469
00:39:50,810 --> 00:39:52,540
Bran the Builder and King Torrhen and--

470
00:39:52,550 --> 00:39:54,950
First things first. It's a long march ahead.

471
00:39:55,280 --> 00:39:56,990
And then we have to take the castle.

472
00:39:57,080 --> 00:39:58,370
Is there going to be a battle?

473
00:39:58,390 --> 00:40:01,060
Aye, Princess, but you won't be anywhere near--

474
00:40:01,060 --> 00:40:03,250
That's enough talk of battle, Ser Davos.

475
00:40:04,240 --> 00:40:05,800
You'll scare the child.

476
00:40:06,400 --> 00:40:07,600
Yes, my queen.

477
00:40:10,670 --> 00:40:13,460
- I'm not scared. - Well, I am.

478
00:40:14,150 --> 00:40:16,610
When the battle comes, promise you'll protect me.

479
00:40:16,610 --> 00:40:17,900
I promise.

480
00:40:38,680 --> 00:40:41,910
I hope you know what you're doing with these wildlings.

481
00:40:42,460 --> 00:40:43,860
I need those ships.

482
00:40:45,180 --> 00:40:48,360
You'll get them back, I swear it.

483
00:40:50,320 --> 00:40:51,700
Have a safe journey, Your Grace.

484
00:40:53,460 --> 00:40:54,700
And thank you.

485
00:41:24,070 --> 00:41:25,340
Mount up!

486
00:41:26,030 --> 00:41:27,220
Colors!

487
00:42:17,250 --> 00:42:18,150
No.

488
00:42:19,730 --> 00:42:21,070
You're still too weak.

489
00:42:32,520 --> 00:42:33,860
Ser Barristan?

490
00:42:59,880 --> 00:43:01,270
Are you ashamed?

491
00:43:03,500 --> 00:43:05,630
You were ambushed, outnumbered.

492
00:43:06,150 --> 00:43:07,650
There was no way you could have known.

493
00:43:07,650 --> 00:43:09,250
This is not why.

494
00:43:12,570 --> 00:43:14,830
Wounded in war,

495
00:43:15,680 --> 00:43:17,560
there is no shame for this.

496
00:43:18,280 --> 00:43:19,820
I am ashamed

497
00:43:20,400 --> 00:43:22,890
because when the knife go in

498
00:43:23,090 --> 00:43:24,940
and I fall to the ground,

499
00:43:26,530 --> 00:43:28,060
I am afraid.

500
00:43:29,870 --> 00:43:31,660
All men fear death.

501
00:43:31,660 --> 00:43:34,210
No, not death.

502
00:43:37,560 --> 00:43:38,770
I fear

503
00:43:39,810 --> 00:43:44,810
I never again see Missandei from the Island of Naath.

504
00:44:21,250 --> 00:44:24,010
Now you have given the Masters what they deserve.

505
00:44:24,010 --> 00:44:25,300
If I give everyone what they deserve,

506
00:44:25,300 --> 00:44:26,920
I'll have no one left to rule.

507
00:44:28,080 --> 00:44:30,160
Ser Barristan counseled mercy

508
00:44:30,170 --> 00:44:33,030
when I took this city right up to the morning he died.

509
00:44:33,490 --> 00:44:36,030
Daario Naharis thinks I should kill the former Masters

510
00:44:36,030 --> 00:44:38,360
and let the rest of the city fend for itself.

511
00:44:39,820 --> 00:44:40,970
What do you think?

512
00:44:42,870 --> 00:44:44,810
Your Grace, I think that I am not fit

513
00:44:44,810 --> 00:44:46,790
to have an opinion on these matters.

514
00:44:47,270 --> 00:44:49,650
You are as fit as anyone I know.

515
00:44:51,290 --> 00:44:53,010
You know why I'm here.

516
00:44:53,670 --> 00:44:56,670
And you know who will suffer the most if this all falls apart.

517
00:44:57,220 --> 00:44:59,130
So what do you think?

518
00:45:02,300 --> 00:45:05,260
I can only tell you what I have seen, Your Grace.

519
00:45:05,830 --> 00:45:08,780
I have seen you listen to your counselors.

520
00:45:10,540 --> 00:45:12,870
I have seen you lean on their experience

521
00:45:12,870 --> 00:45:14,470
when your own was lacking

522
00:45:14,510 --> 00:45:17,070
and weigh the choices they put before you.

523
00:45:19,300 --> 00:45:21,890
And I have seen you ignore your counselors...

524
00:45:24,730 --> 00:45:26,870
because there was a better choice.

525
00:45:27,570 --> 00:45:29,560
One that only you could see.

526
00:45:46,760 --> 00:45:49,230
My-- my queen, please do not do this.

527
00:45:49,810 --> 00:45:51,420
What about "Valar morghulis"?

528
00:45:51,920 --> 00:45:54,070
I did not want to die a coward.

529
00:45:59,250 --> 00:46:01,640
Apparently I do not want to die at all.

530
00:46:04,090 --> 00:46:05,880
It takes courage to admit fear.

531
00:46:07,630 --> 00:46:09,330
And to admit a mistake.

532
00:46:11,400 --> 00:46:13,510
I came here to tell you that I was wrong.

533
00:46:16,830 --> 00:46:19,200
I was wrong and you were right.

534
00:46:21,200 --> 00:46:22,570
About tradition.

535
00:46:24,960 --> 00:46:27,420
About bringing the people of this city together.

536
00:46:31,320 --> 00:46:33,230
I will reopen the fighting pits.

537
00:46:34,090 --> 00:46:35,870
To free men only.

538
00:46:36,110 --> 00:46:40,200
Slavery will never return to Meereen, not while I live.

539
00:46:40,200 --> 00:46:41,630
Yes, my queen.

540
00:46:45,640 --> 00:46:49,580
And in order to forge a lasting bond with the Meereenese people,

541
00:46:49,890 --> 00:46:52,440
I will marry the leader of an ancient family.

542
00:46:54,800 --> 00:46:57,530
Thankfully a suitor is already on his knees.

543
00:47:25,910 --> 00:47:27,070
Don't worry.

544
00:47:27,920 --> 00:47:30,890
I'll be fine. Nothing broken, I don't think.

545
00:47:33,520 --> 00:47:34,790
Where are we now?

546
00:47:35,300 --> 00:47:36,730
Not the Rhoyne.

547
00:47:43,280 --> 00:47:45,790
Long, sullen silences

548
00:47:45,790 --> 00:47:48,760
and an occasional punch in the face.

549
00:47:50,860 --> 00:47:52,530
The Mormont way.

550
00:47:56,370 --> 00:47:58,710
Let's start over.

551
00:48:00,450 --> 00:48:02,740
I apologize for before.

552
00:48:02,950 --> 00:48:05,600
My mouth sometimes runs away from me.

553
00:48:06,230 --> 00:48:08,640
This doesn't have to be an unpleasant trip.

554
00:48:13,840 --> 00:48:16,590
We're going to be spending a lot of time together on the way to Meereen.

555
00:48:16,910 --> 00:48:17,830
We are.

556
00:48:20,140 --> 00:48:23,020
What would make our time together truly enjoyable

557
00:48:23,020 --> 00:48:24,350
would be some wine.

558
00:48:25,980 --> 00:48:27,120
No wine.

559
00:48:29,670 --> 00:48:33,070
I am a person who drinks.

560
00:48:34,970 --> 00:48:37,350
People who drink need to keep drinking.

561
00:48:37,360 --> 00:48:38,970
Otherwise, they're not...

562
00:48:46,830 --> 00:48:48,010
I know where we are.

563
00:48:48,400 --> 00:48:50,260
You're taking us through Valyria.

564
00:48:51,290 --> 00:48:52,260
I am.

565
00:48:52,940 --> 00:48:54,420
Have you sailed this route before?

566
00:48:54,470 --> 00:48:55,240
No.

567
00:48:56,310 --> 00:48:57,920
You're going to bring Daenerys a souvenir

568
00:48:57,930 --> 00:49:00,380
from her ancestral homeland in case I'm not enough?

569
00:49:00,770 --> 00:49:02,340
I think you'll be plenty.

570
00:49:03,860 --> 00:49:05,310
You know what they say.

571
00:49:06,430 --> 00:49:08,660
The Doom still rules Valyria.

572
00:49:09,650 --> 00:49:12,050
What about the demons and the flames?

573
00:49:13,310 --> 00:49:14,790
Aren't you afraid of the Doom?

574
00:49:15,400 --> 00:49:16,210
No.

575
00:49:17,710 --> 00:49:19,030
But pirates are.

576
00:49:24,870 --> 00:49:26,720
The Smoking Sea.

577
00:49:28,500 --> 00:49:30,270
How many centuries before we learn

578
00:49:30,270 --> 00:49:32,360
how to build cities like this again?

579
00:49:33,710 --> 00:49:36,130
For thousands of years the valyrians were

580
00:49:36,340 --> 00:49:39,550
the best in the world at almost everything.

581
00:49:40,350 --> 00:49:41,170
And then...

582
00:49:42,330 --> 00:49:43,670
And then they weren't.

583
00:49:45,210 --> 00:49:46,350
And then they weren't.

584
00:49:50,200 --> 00:49:54,290
"They held each other close and turned their backs upon the end.

585
00:49:55,030 --> 00:49:56,870
The hills that split asunder

586
00:49:57,340 --> 00:49:59,440
and the black that ate the skies;

587
00:50:00,020 --> 00:50:02,220
The flames that shot so high and hot

588
00:50:02,220 --> 00:50:03,960
that even dragons burned;

589
00:50:04,170 --> 00:50:06,300
Would never be the final sights

590
00:50:06,300 --> 00:50:08,020
that fell upon their eyes.

591
00:50:09,630 --> 00:50:11,100
A fly upon a wall,

592
00:50:11,680 --> 00:50:15,600
the waves the sea wind whipped and churned--"

593
00:50:15,680 --> 00:50:17,960
"The city of a thousand years,

594
00:50:18,410 --> 00:50:20,350
and all that men had learned;

595
00:50:20,730 --> 00:50:23,310
The Doom consumed it all alike,

596
00:50:24,200 --> 00:50:26,140
and neither of them turned."

597
00:50:29,390 --> 00:50:30,670
I would clap.

598
00:50:37,010 --> 00:50:38,800
I suppose this is it, then.

599
00:50:40,550 --> 00:50:42,190
This is what remains.

600
00:51:22,140 --> 00:51:23,290
What was that?

601
00:51:30,570 --> 00:51:31,880
Stone Men!

602
00:51:32,160 --> 00:51:33,650
Don't let them touch you!

603
00:51:50,410 --> 00:51:51,500
Get behind!

604
00:51:54,770 --> 00:51:56,690
Mormont, cut me free!

605
00:51:57,550 --> 00:51:58,530
Mormont!

606
00:52:14,150 --> 00:52:15,120
Mormont!

607
00:52:16,270 --> 00:52:17,420
Mormont!

608
00:52:53,850 --> 00:52:54,740
Tyrion?

609
00:52:58,830 --> 00:52:59,700
Tyrion.

610
00:53:01,520 --> 00:53:02,370
Tyrion.

611
00:53:04,370 --> 00:53:05,240
Tyrion.

612
00:53:07,570 --> 00:53:08,680
You're all right.

613
00:53:19,110 --> 00:53:20,680
You're heavier than you look.

614
00:53:23,890 --> 00:53:25,420
Did any of them touch you?

615
00:53:29,160 --> 00:53:30,030
You?

616
00:53:36,050 --> 00:53:37,710
I've seen greyscale before,

617
00:53:39,010 --> 00:53:40,260
but nothing like that.

618
00:53:40,990 --> 00:53:42,980
I suppose that's why they send them there.

619
00:53:45,230 --> 00:53:47,080
It'd be kinder to put daggers in their hearts

620
00:53:47,080 --> 00:53:48,290
and be done with it.

621
00:53:52,860 --> 00:53:55,890
Thank you for saving me.

622
00:53:59,280 --> 00:54:01,250
Of course, I wouldn't have needed saving

623
00:54:01,250 --> 00:54:03,370
if you hadn't kidnapped me in the first place.

624
00:54:07,910 --> 00:54:09,920
So what now?

625
00:54:09,980 --> 00:54:12,020
We walk up the coast.

626
00:54:12,020 --> 00:54:14,130
With luck, we'll find a fishing village.

627
00:54:14,870 --> 00:54:15,980
Maybe another boat.

628
00:54:16,400 --> 00:54:17,430
Without luck?

629
00:54:18,510 --> 00:54:20,260
We've got a long walk ahead of us.

630
00:54:23,370 --> 00:54:25,330
I'll get some wood for a fire.

631
00:54:26,250 --> 00:54:27,820
Try to get some rest, huh?

632
00:54:29,310 --> 00:54:31,680
That's the best idea you've had all day.

